      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would not work. Once instance where we see this problem is when calling EthernetManager#setEthernetEnabled(false), which untracks / removes all interfaces from the factory. The link state of these interfaces hasn\u0027t changed, so mLinkUp is still true. NetworkProvider#unregisterNetwork() which is called as part of removeInterface() executes asynchronously, so onNetworkNeeded callbacks can still be received even \"after\" the offer is unregistered. Samsung has actually encountered this problem during testing (b/171872016#comment70). This could of course also happen if link state went down and came right back up (at which point we could also receive onNetworkNeeded callbacks on the stale object).\n\nThis is really the exact same issue that we had with IpClientCallbacks and presumably at some point also the NetworkAgent callbacks. 😞\nThis is intermittently fixed in NetworkProvider (aosp/2148674), but I would like to revert that change (and add more documentation instead) as it is not a generic fix for all threading models.",
